# GMM00010035-data-beg2026.txt.zip

Dataset: ref-igra — Every 2026 radiosonde sounding of IGRA 2 (NOAA NCEI, ~800 stations, twice
  daily): the refraction coefficient k of the measured air, day and night
File: data/ref/igra/raw/GMM00010035-data-beg2026.txt.zip
SHA-256: 2578e168bd0ed70b30c3372d26d9940b07c38b1bbedfe020cb409f4aa322175c (also in
  data/ref/igra/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/ref/igra && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: the file may be shared but is kept
  out of git for its size. Get it from fog fetch ref-igra, then compare its SHA-256 with the one
  above.
Obtained: downloaded as published (fog fetch or by hand).
From: NOAA NCEI, IGRA 2 current-year file of each station (data-y2d), downloaded once (fog fetch
  ref-igra).
Collected: 2026-10-28
Licence: public-domain
Sources:
- I. Durre, X. Yin, R. S. Vose, S. Applequist and J. Arnfield, Enhancing the Data Coverage in the
  Integrated Global Radiosonde Archive, J. Atmos. Oceanic Technol. 35 (2018) 1753-1770; IGRA version
  2, NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information
  <https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/data/integrated-global-radiosonde-archive/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- k: k = R/ρ is the ray's curvature divided by the Earth's: the radius is its unit (503 = R ·
  78.8e-6)
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Air in which k ≥ 1 (a ray curving as much as the
  ground, the globe looking flat) in most soundings, in every climate, by day and by night.
